       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is five times the labeled maximum daily dose for adults, which is 10 mg. Nothing in the patient details you gave (70 kg, normal kidney and liver function) would justify a dose that high. An overdose could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged peripheral vasodilation.\n\nPlease check whether 50 mg was a typo. Here are some options:\n- **5 mg orally once daily.** This is the usual starting dose.\n- **10 mg orally once daily.** This is the maximum dose.\n\nIf you want one of these, tell me the dose and I'll enter it right away. If you meant a different drug or dose, let me know. If you need a higher level of blood pressure control, adding a second agent from another class is the usual approach, and pharmacy or the attending can help choose one."
